title: Wi_Start_Day1
position: -83,-166
---

<<declare $widg_joinedcircus=false>>
<<declare $widg_murderday=false>>
<<declare $widg_normalday=false>>
<<declare $widg_victim=false>>



???: *In front of you stands a slim but muscular young monkey. His frown forms a curious paradox with the stressed look in his eyes.*
You: Hello.
???: H... Hello.
???: Boss said someone is coming to tell who killed Mister Waddles.
???: Widget saw you walking round the wagon talking to others.
???: *Gulps * Boss said you need to talk to Widget.
You: *Take out your notebook* I take it you are Widget?
Widget: *slightly shivers* Widget is Widget.
You: See, Mr. Widget...
You: As a detective investigating the case, I talk to everyone.
    -> You: There is no reason to worry.
        Widget: *shift his weight from one leg to another* Widget knows. It's just...
    -> You: Only the murderer needs to worry.
        Widget: *his eyes get bigger* Murde- ... Widget knows. It's just...
Widget: Widget doesn’t talk face-to-face with people a lot.
Widget: People stay down there and cheer and clap when Widgets up in the air *his face glows* is nice.
    -> You: That does sound nice.
        Widget: *Smiles*
    -> You: That sounds horrible.
        Widget: *Nods understandingly* scary for detective, safe for Widget. widget knows what widget is doing.
You: Right. I assume you’re one of the monkey acrobats?
You: I have some questions for you. Just getting the general idea... 
Widget: *shift uncomfortably* widget helps the best widget can. 
You: Let's start with a simple one. Can you tell me why you joined the circus?

<<jump Widg_JoinedCircus>>

===
title: Widget_Day_One
---
<<declare $widge_nap_waddles to false>>
<<declare $widge_nap to false>>


<<if ($widg_murderday and $widg_normalday and $widg_victim)>>
    You: You can indeed go now, Mr. Widget. Thank you for your time.
    You: Anything you might want to share with me?
    <<wait  1.5>>
    You: Mr. Widget?
    Widget: *tries to stand as tall as he can* Widget has said all there is to say.
    <<stop>>
<<elseif ($widg_murderday and $widg_normalday) or ($widg_murderday and $widg_victim) or ($widg_normalday and $widg_victim)>>
    You: We are almost done Mr. Widget.
<<else>>
    Widget: Can Widget go now?
    You: Just a few more minutes of your time, Mr. Widget...
<<endif>>
-> You: *Turn a page in your notebook* How about you tell me about your boss a bit? <<if $widge_nap is false and $widge_nap_waddles is true>>
    <<jump Widge_Nap>>
-> You: What does a regular circus day for you look like? <<if $widg_normalday is false>>
    <<jump Widg_NormalDay>>
-> You: What were you doing on the day of the murder? <<if $widg_murderday is false>>
    <<jump Widg_MurderDay>>
-> You: How well did you know the victim? <<if $widg_victim is false>>
    <<jump Widg_Victim>> 
-> You: Actually, I think that's enough for today.
    You: Anything you might want to share with me?
    <<wait  1.5>>
    You: Mr. Widget?
    Widget: *tries to stand as tall as he can* Widget has said all there is to say.
    <<stop>>
===
title: Widg_Victim
---
<<set $widge_nap_waddles to true>>
<<set $widg_victim to true>>

Widget: *thinks* Mr. Waddles was a gentleman. Smelled nice. Had nice things. Knew many words.
Widget: Mr. Waddles smoked a lot. Widget didn’t understand—didn’t he need his lungs to play the trumpet?
Widget: *pauses. looks frustrated* Mr. Waddles didn’t take very good care of himself. 
Widget: *holds his breath and flexes his muscles* Widget takes very good care of himself.
You: I can see that Mr. Widget.
Widget: *lets go of his breath* Wiiiiidget didn’t really know him closely. He didn’t talk to Widget as much. He was an artist. *looks wistful*
    -> You: What you do is a form of art too, Mr. Widget.
        Widget: That’s what Lady Poppet says. She says, "Widget..."
        Widget: She says, "What we do is art defined. we dance up there, we give our hearts to the audience... like we're showing them everything."
        Widget: *Pauses* Lady Poppet’s phrasing is more pretty.
        You: I got the idea.
    -> You: You wanted to be an artist too?
        Widget: *shrugs* Widget didn’t want to be an artist until Mr. Waddles told Widget he isn’t one.
        Widget: Widget just wanted to be widget.
        Widget: *His eyes darken* But what if it’s not enough?
        Widget: lady poppet says. she says widget...
        Widget: She says "What we do is art defined. we dance up there, we give our hearts to the audience... like we're showing them everything."
        Widget: *Pauses* Lady Poppet phrases is more pretty. Our bodies are our brushes. Or something like that?
        You: I got the idea.
You: So I can safely conclude that you and the victim were not friends?
Widget: Sir... Madam detective... Erm, Your Majesty...
You: Detective is enough, Mr. Widget.
Widget: Detective... Widget doesn’t think Mr. Waddles had any friends.
Widget: *thinks* Mr. Eduard did talk to him sometimes. So did Boss.
Widget: Boss rarely looked happy about talking to him.
Widget: Mr. Eduard never looked happy about talking to him.
Widget: Widget wonders if that's just how Mr. Eduard looks.
Widget: Widget was happy for Mr. Eduard... Mr. Eduard lives inside his head. Seems like a lonely place.
Widget: *taps his temple* Widget doesn’t think that’s a nice place to be, Mr. Eduard's head.
    -> You: What gets *you* out of your head, Widget?
        Widget: Jumping. High. In the Air. And Lady Poppet.
        Widget: *his face lightens* Lady Poppet is widget's best friend.
        Widget: Widget would jump very very high for Lady Poppet.
            <<jump Widget_Day_One>>
    -> You: Do *you* have friends, Widget?
        Widget: *his face lightens* Lady Poppet is widget's best friend.
        Widget: Widget would jump very very high for Lady Poppet.
            <<jump Widget_Day_One>>


===
title: Widg_NormalDay
---

Widget: Widget practices all day. Widget is very good at what Widget does...
Widget: *nods knowingly* because he practices all day.
You: ...
You: And?
Widget: *looks confused* That’s a normal day for Widget.
Widget: Widget also washes his hair. *thinks* Not everyday. *thinks* Unless it's summer.
You: That makes sense, Mr. Widget.
Widget: He also sleeps... very late. Because Mr. Waddles likes to play his trumpet when everyone’s gone to bed.
Widget: Sleep... will be easier now. *looks guilty* Not that Widget’s happy about what it took...
    -> You: It's OK, Widget. Sleep is very important.
        You: Apart from that, was there any other way the deceased made life harder for others?
        Widget: *counts with his fingers* ... yes.
    -> You: Would you say anyone got angrier than usual about the late-night rehearsals?
        You: Or... angry about any other ways Mr. Waddles made things harder for others?
        Widget: *thinks, then points to his chest* 
        <<wait 1>> 
        Widget: Widget?
        You: Yes. Other than you.
Widget: Widget doesn’t like talkin' bad about dead people... *looks uncomfortable*
Widget: Mr. Waddles... wasn’t a very nice man. *hesitates* He took other people’s stuff... without asking.
Widget: Widget never does that... or, at least... feels very, very bad about it.
Widget: He made Widget feel bad. Talked bad about the circus. That’s not fair. The circus is home.
Widget: *sighs* Maybe he was right to do so? *pauses* He seemed... very wealthy. Like, from a proper home. Went to school and all that.
    -> You: Why would he join a circus, then?
        Widget: *shrugs* Widget never asked.
        Widget: But it’s nice here... you see the world, make people happy, there’s food and a place to sleep...
        Widget: *looks confused* What more do people want?
    -> You: Wealthy, well-educated people don’t usually join a traveling circus.
        Widget: *looks sad*
        You:  No offense. They also don’t usually become detectives.
            Widget: But it’s nice here... you see the world, make people happy, there’s food and a place to sleep...
            Widget: *looks confused* what more do people want? 
    <<set $widg_normalday to true>>
    <<jump Widget_Day_One>>
===
title: Widg_MurderDay
---

Widget: *Face brightens* Widget practiced all day.
You: Did you notice anything unusual between your sessions?
Widget: *thinks* ...Widget and Lady Poppet trained in the morning. Then Lady Poppet made sandwiches.
Widget: Then Widget ate his sandwich.
<<wait 0.5>> 
You: *wait patiently*
<<wait 0.5>> 
Widget: ...After, Widget and Lady Poppet watched Mr. Eduard and Mr. Teddy practice their new routine.
Widget: *nods* Was not going well. 
Widget: Then Widget went for his afternoon run, took a bath, did his hair,
    -> You: *look at his hair enviously and say nothing*
    ->Y ou: You do have impressive hair, Mr. Widget.
        Widget: *Blushes* Widget tries his best. 
    Widget: Widget can share his hair routine with the detective.
        -> You: Err, another time, perhaps.
        -> You: I don't need a new routine... *push your hand in your hair expectantly*
    Widget: *Stares at your head. Looks worried* That's what Mr. Eduard said.
    Widget: ... Where was widget? *thinks*
Widget: Then straight to wagon. Then beauty sleep. 
Widget: No trumpet sound. Widget was happy caus did not know why there was no trumpet sound. *Looks apologetic.*
Widget: Nothing unusual. *avoids eye contact*
<<set $widg_murderday to true>>
<<jump Widget_Day_One>>

===
title: Widg_JoinedCircus
---
    Widget: *looks proud* Yes.
    Widget: Food and a place to sleep.
        -> You: ... Thats it?
            Widget: *looks confused* Is that not enough?
            Widget: *shrugs*  Widget also likes makin’ people happy, or cheer, or hold their breath.
            Widget: Widget likes people, as long as they are very far.
        -> You: That makes sense.
            Widget: *nods* Widget can talk to the Boss, put in good word—if detective wants.
            Widget: *eyes you up and down* How far can detective jump?
                -> You: Awfully low.
                -> You: Very high.
                Widget: *opens his arms* Detective and Widget can train together!
                You: Very nice, Widget. But back to my question…
                Widget: *shrugs* Widget likes makin’ people happy, or cheer, or hold their breath.
                Widget: *flexes his muscles* Nothing can stop Widget when he is on the stage...
You: Understood. And...
    -> You: How long have you been here?
    -> You: Do you see yourself staying after all this?
Widget: *hugs his tail* Widget joined circus in early days.
Widget: When Widget was a small monkey, and Boss was a kitten…
Widget: *pauses*  Don’t tell him Widget said that.
Widget: And Widget’s gonna stay here 'til long strong hands get too old to grab the pole.
<<set $widg_joinedcircus to true>>
<<jump Widget_Day_One>>
===
title: Widge_Nap
---
<<set $widge_nap to true>>
You: You mentioned knowing him since childhood.
Widget: *Nods cautiosly*
You: What can you tell me about him?
Widget: *Thinks*
<<wait  1>>
Widget: Widget can help better if detective asks questions.
You: Very well. 
    -> You: What kind of a man is he? I mean...
        Widget: *Looks confused*
        You: Alright. Lets break this down. Can you describe him in three words for me?
        Widget: *thinks*
        <<wait  2>>
        Widget: Boss hates taxes. *looks proud*
        <<wait  1>>
        Widget: *Looks at your expression, confused* Three words. Boss... Hates... *starts counting with his fingers*
        You: You're right Widget. Thank you for this useful information.
        -> You: I recall you said your boss did talk with the late Mr. Waddles from time to time.
        -> You: How was the relationship between your boss and Mr. Waddles?
        Widget: *Cautiously* yes?
        You: *take a deep breath*
        -> You: Can you elaborate, Mr. Widget?
        <<wait  2>>
        Widget: No.
        You: *Sigh*
        <<jump Widget_Day_One>>

